{
  "_doc": "Reactome (five headerless TSVs, CC0): the Pathway node, the PART_OF_PATHWAY hierarchy and the Metabolite-[:IN_PATHWAY]->Pathway edge joined to HMDB's chebi_id. The hierarchy is a DAG (388 children have more than one parent), so no cardinality cap is declared on it. IN_PATHWAY is declared under Metabolite as an addition to blueprints/hmdb.json's node, and blueprints/kegg.json declares the same junction because both sources write rows into one CSV — one relationship, one file, two contributors. NCBI2Reactome is NCBI *Gene*, not taxonomy, and is not loaded.",
  "_files": "Every table this fragment reads, declared once. A frame the build hands over by name; the preps fill it, nothing on disk backs it.",
